ARTICLES=[
('emergency-fence-rental-indiana-same-week-perimeter-fencing-after-storms-fires-and-break-ins','Emergency Fencing After Property Damage','What to have ready when a commercial property needs a temporary perimeter after a storm, fire, vehicle strike, or break-in.','windscreen.jpg',[
('Start with the location and access',['An emergency fence request often begins before anyone has a complete plan. Give Richard the site address, describe what happened, and explain which areas need to be closed off. Approximate dimensions are enough to begin the conversation.','Tell him whether crews, adjusters, inspectors, or deliveries still need to enter. Also mention any restrictions on truck access or unloading. Those details help determine where the run and gates should go.']),
('Choose a system for the restoration work',['Panels on weighted stands are often the quickest way to establish a temporary boundary. They can follow an irregular site and move as cleanup or restoration progresses.','For a longer closure with a fixed perimeter, post-driven chain link may be a better fit. The choice depends on the ground, how often access changes, and how long the work is expected to last. Screen can be added where reducing visibility into the site is useful.']),
('Confirm a real installation time',['The normal installation window is 24–48 hours. Emergency work may move faster, but availability depends on the location, current jobs, and equipment on hand. Call Richard to confirm an arrival plan for your site.','An inquiry sent through the form provides useful details, but an urgent perimeter is worth a phone call. Describe the deadline clearly so it can be discussed before the crew is scheduled.']),
('Allow for the next phase',['Think beyond the first day. Debris removal, equipment delivery, and later reconstruction may need different access. Let Richard know what is likely to change so the fence plan can account for it.','Fence Wizards provides temporary fencing rather than permanent fence repair. If damaged permanent fencing also needs work, that is a separate service.']),
('Understand the rental terms',['The quote includes delivery, installation, rental for the agreed term, and removal. Standard terms run up to 12 months, with shorter-job pricing available. Contact Richard before the agreed term ends if restoration will take longer.','Fence Wizards carries umbrella, general liability, commercial auto, and workers compensation insurance. Ask about any certificates the restoration contractor or property manager needs.'])],['/emergency-fencing/','/fence/panels-and-stands/','/pricing/']),
('how-a-temporary-fence-rental-works','How a Temporary Fence Rental Works','From the first project details to installation and final pickup: what to expect when renting from Fence Wizards.','panels.jpg',[
('Bring the details you have',['A quote starts with five things: location, fence type, approximate linear footage, gates, and rental duration. If you do not know the right system or exact measurements, start with the address and a description of the job.','A site plan is helpful but not required for the first conversation. Mark where deliveries arrive and where people need to pass through the boundary.']),
('Choose panels or a driven line',['Panels stand above the surface in weighted bases and can move as the layout changes. They work on paved ground as well as other suitable surfaces.','Post-driven chain link uses posts set into the ground for a more fixed perimeter. It takes more installation work and is less convenient to relocate. Ground conditions and the project phases help determine the right choice.']),
('Agree on the price and schedule',['Richard can discuss a verbal quote on the phone and follow with a written proposal. The flat fee includes delivery, installation, rental for the agreed term, and removal.','Vetted commercial accounts can use Net 30. Smaller or unvetted accounts pay up front. The applicable terms are agreed at the start. Installation usually falls within 24–48 hours; confirm the actual date for your job.']),
('Keep in touch while the fence is up',['Call when the layout changes or a gate is in the way. General contractors receive same-day service for changes on existing jobs. Your crew can move individual portable panels; larger moves or driven-fence changes need the installation crew.','Standard rentals cover up to 12 months. A schedule slip inside the agreed term does not create a monthly rent charge. Discuss extensions before that term ends and ask about pricing if the scope changes.']),
('Arrange pickup',['Tell Richard when the area is ready and whether anything has changed about access for the truck. Removal was included in the quote.','For an event, provide the load-out time while planning the rental so the fencing can be removed when the event ends.'])],['/pricing/','/fence/panels-and-stands/','/contact/']),
('how-much-does-temporary-fence-rental-cost','What Affects Temporary Fence Rental Cost?','How fence type, footage, gates, site access, and rental length shape your quote—and what Fence Wizards includes.','construction.jpg',[
('Fence Wizards quotes a flat fee',['Fence Wizards prices the job for an agreed term. Delivery, installation, and removal are included. The standard rental runs up to 12 months, and short jobs of a few months or less receive discounted pricing.','This is why a monthly price per foot does not describe the whole offer. Ask for a quote based on your actual site and scope, then compare what is included.']),
('Fence type and installation work',['Panels and stands are fast to install and move. They are often the practical starting point for a changing site, a paved lot, or an event.','Post-driven chain link involves driving posts and hanging the fabric. That additional labor affects the quote. It can be useful for a longer fixed boundary where portability is less important.']),
('Footage, gates, and duration',['The total run determines how much material and installation work are needed. Rough measurements are useful at the start; a site plan can help refine them.','Gate count and position matter too. A wide delivery entrance and several pedestrian openings create a different layout from a simple closed perimeter. Tell Richard what needs to enter and where.','Include the expected duration even if the completion date is provisional. Short-term work can be priced differently from a standard rental.']),
('Ground, access, and distance',['A truck that can unload beside the run makes a different installation from a tight frontage where material needs carrying. Paved ground, rock, slopes, and fill also affect the fencing system and the work required.','Travel to a site near the edge of the service area is included in the quoted number and discussed with you. Give the full address early.']),
('Compare the complete quote',['Check the agreed rental term, delivery, installation, removal, and any additional items. Windscreen is sold rather than rented, so include it when comparing scopes.','Richard can review a written quote from another company and explain how the Fence Wizards offer compares. The family-owned operation and direct material purchasing help keep pricing competitive.']),
('Changes after the quote',['A delay within the agreed rental term does not change the rental fee. If the term needs extending, call before it ends. Added footage, gates, or other scope changes should be discussed with Richard.','Net 30 is available for vetted accounts. Smaller or unvetted accounts pay up front, with the applicable terms explained at the start. PlotQuote is coming soon; use the contact form or call for a quote in the meantime.'])],['/pricing/','/fence/post-driven-chain-link/','/contact/']),
('post-driven-chain-link-fence-rental-flood-repair-public-works-hamilton-marion-county','Choosing Fencing for Public Works & Flood Repair','Planning a fixed or changing perimeter for repair work in Hamilton and Marion counties.','chain-link.jpg',[
('Begin with the work boundary',['A repair site may run beside an active sidewalk, road, or public property. Share the planned work boundary, pedestrian routes, and equipment access with Richard.','The fencing choice should follow the site plan and project requirements. Identify what will remain fixed and what will change as the work progresses.']),
('When a driven line fits',['Post-driven chain link can suit a longer project with a stable perimeter. The posts are driven into the ground and the fabric is tensioned along the line, making it less portable than panels.','It requires suitable ground. Rock, heavy fill, and underground utilities can affect where posts may go and how the line is installed. Share known ground conditions early.']),
('When portable panels help',['Panels and weighted stands can be useful on paved surfaces or where the work zone needs to move. Individual sections can be shifted as access changes.','Some projects call for both systems: driven fencing on fixed boundaries and panels in areas that need flexibility. Explain the phases rather than choosing one system for the entire job before discussing the site.']),
('Plan equipment access before the fence',['Mark the entry points for excavation equipment, material deliveries, and debris removal. Gate locations matter especially on a driven line, because changes require a crew visit.','If screening is needed along a public-facing edge, include it in the quote. Windscreen changes the load on the supporting fence and should be considered as part of the installation.']),
('Coordinate the schedule and paperwork',['Fence Wizards serves Hamilton and Marion counties from Greenwood. Installation normally takes place within 24–48 hours, with emergency timing confirmed directly with Richard.','Ask about insurance certificates required for the job. Quotes include delivery, installation, the agreed rental term, and removal; standard rentals cover up to 12 months.'])],['/fence/post-driven-chain-link/','/construction-fencing/','/service-area/noblesville/']),
('printed-windscreen-for-construction-fence-indianapolis-branding-privacy-dust-control','Planning Printed Windscreen for Your Fence','What to consider when adding privacy, dust screening, and project graphics to a temporary perimeter.','printed-screen.jpg',[
('What windscreen adds',['Windscreen is fabric fitted across a chain link fence run. Plain screen reduces the view into a construction or service area. Printed screen can also carry a company name, sponsor, development rendering, or leasing message.','Both versions are sold, not rented. The screen stays yours when the temporary fence is collected.']),
('Privacy and dust at the perimeter',['Screen can reduce visibility into a site where tools, material, or restoration work would otherwise be on view. On a busy street, it also changes what the public sees along the boundary.','It can help limit dust leaving the perimeter, but it does not replace other dust-control measures used on the job. Explain the purpose of the screen when talking with Richard.']),
('Plan the supporting fence',['Screen adds wind load. The fence system, weighting, exposure, and ground conditions need to be considered together. Let Richard know early if the run will be screened.','Screen fits both panels and post-driven chain link. It can also be added later, but the existing support needs to be assessed rather than treating it as a purely visual addition.']),
('Make the graphics useful',['Decide who will see the fence and from where. A company name and clear contact information may suit a construction frontage; an event perimeter may need sponsor artwork.','Provide the fence height, printed area, artwork, and required date. The design needs to work across the actual run, including gates and other breaks. Discuss production details before setting an installation deadline.']),
('Ordering and keeping the screen',['Ask for plain and printed options if you are weighing the value of graphics. Include windscreen in the scope when comparing fence quotes.','If you want screen fitted to fencing already installed by someone else, describe the existing run to Richard. The fit and support determine whether the work is suitable.'])],['/fence/windscreen/','/event-fencing/','/construction-fencing/']),
('temporary-fence-panels-for-rent-in-indianapolis-fast-setup-flexible-configuratio-1788192322725','When Temporary Fence Panels Are the Right Fit','Portable panels for construction phases, event footprints, and sites where driven posts are unsuitable.','panels.jpg',[
('How panels and stands work',['Freestanding panels sit in bases weighted with sandbags. They form a temporary boundary above the ground without driven posts, which makes them useful on concrete, asphalt, and other suitable surfaces.','Fence Wizards carries six-foot panels, with eight-foot options available. Ask about the required height when quoting so availability can be confirmed.']),
('For a site that changes',['Panels are useful when the construction layout changes between phases. A crew can move individual sections to adjust an access point; larger relocations can be handled by Fence Wizards.','That flexibility also suits events, where a perimeter goes in during load-in and comes out after the event. Barricades can be rented alongside panels for queues or other areas within the footprint.']),
('Plan the access points',['Tell Richard where deliveries arrive and what must pass through each entrance. Pedestrian and drive gates can be included in the run.','Avoid treating gate positions as whatever space is left after the fence is laid out. The access plan should help determine the boundary from the start.']),
('Screening and site exposure',['Plain or custom printed windscreen can be fitted for privacy, dust control, or graphics. It is sold separately and remains yours after the rental.','Screen increases wind load. The location, support, and weighting need to be considered together, so mention screening requirements before installation.']),
('When to choose something more fixed',['Panels are portable by design. Where the perimeter will stay in one place for a long period and portability is a drawback, consider post-driven chain link.','The choice also depends on whether the ground accepts posts. Richard can discuss both systems using the location, approximate footage, gate plan, and expected duration.']),
('Quote, setup, and pickup',['The normal installation window is 24–48 hours, with panels often possible sooner. Confirm your date directly with Richard.','The flat-fee quote includes installation and removal for the agreed term. Standard rentals cover up to 12 months, with short-term discounts available.'])],['/fence/panels-and-stands/','/fence/post-driven-chain-link/','/pricing/'])]
